1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,593
Welcome to the build!

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,267
First, the adapter case.

3
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:10,472
I designed this case in my own 3D editor,
called 3table.

4
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:18,228
The board slots into place, with vents and
connectors lining up.

5
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:27,148
And the finished case comes together, lid
and all.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,010
Every board and standoff has its place.

7
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:40,835
Next, the firmware, straight from the
gist.

8
00:00:41,035 --> 00:00:46,088
We include the Joystick library and define
the throttle and steering pins.

9
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:53,065
In setup, we enable the pins and set the X
and Y axis ranges.

10
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:01,181
And in the loop, pulseIn reads each
channel and feeds the joystick axes.

11
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:07,419
Now, the tricky part. Let's test it.

12
00:01:07,619 --> 00:01:12,161
I was recording the video with one hand
and steering with the other.

13
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:20,519
Driving one-handed was not easy, but it
works! RACELOGIC timing keeps score as the

14
00:01:20,519 --> 00:01:21,552
laps come in.
